title: Nkosi Sikelel' iAfrika
artist: Enoch Sontonga
origin: South Africa
culture: South African
genre: Hymn
language: xh
key: G major
tempo: 76
meter: 4/4
pickup: 0
intro: 2
outro: 1
style: hymn
guide: ooh
year: 1897
attribution: Words and music by Enoch Sontonga, a Xhosa mission-school teacher, written in 1897 (he died in 1905), so both are public domain. This is his original first stanza, sung twice; the wording used in today's South African anthem differs in a few words. Melody from his four-part setting, transposed from B flat.
source_url: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nkosi_Sikelel%27_iAfrika.png
tags: south africa, xhosa, hymn, anthem, africa, prayer

